{
  "campaign": "expedition_posting_v2",
  "description": "Measure, on the merged post-#506 model, two quantities on the expedition hull and nothing else: (1) how often a voyage reaches the VSP reporting threshold, and (2) the reported passenger attack rate among the voyages that do. The composed direct-contact route (#506) replaced whole-body per-epoch emission with a finite donor-hand reservoir, added Liu-derived host-level hand-carriage intermittency, switched activity-resolved contact generation on, and gave the emesis aerosol a source-zone dose, so every posting frequency and conditional attack rate recorded before that merge was measured on a different transmission chain and none of them is carried forward here. Nothing in this manifest is fitted: the dose scale is swept as a declared physical release rate (environmental_faecal_release_log10_g_per_epoch, the legacy dose_adjustment key, -log10 grams of stool released to the environment per epoch) and the readout is reported stratified by it, because the ledger's item 00 records a switch in that exponent near adj 6-7 on the pre-merge chain and forbids reading a posting frequency marginalised across it. The shipped norwalk_gi value (4.0) is one rung of the ladder and carries no privileged status. Voyage length is swept because the observed A9 posting probability is strongly length-dependent (0.33 per 1,000 voyages at 6-7 days against 18.3 at 11-14; midrs_incidence_targets.a9_targets), so a single 168-epoch arm cannot be compared with a fleet-pooled target. Comparators are reported and never optimised against: A4 expedition pre-2020 reported passenger AR over postings (median 5.32 percent, IQR 4.00-10.45, n=21) and the A9 fleet interval (4.19-5.58 per 1,000 voyages) with its length-resolved rows. Containment is a separate axis at the shipped rung so that a change in posting frequency stays attributable to either transmission or quarantine compliance rather than to their product; none_response carries sick_call_probability_per_day 0.0 and is the transmission-only counterfactual, not a posting arm. Cell sizes here are set by AWS Batch capacity rather than by a local core count, and the campaign is deliberately unbalanced: 200 voyages per curve cell resolve a posting frequency to roughly plus or minus 0.035 near 0.5 and roughly plus or minus 0.03 near 0.05, which is enough to locate the release rung at which posting stops being a near-certainty and to measure the conditional attack rate, while the shipped rung 4.0 carries 1,000 voyages at both voyage lengths because that is the only cell compared against an observed posting probability. Even 1,000 voyages fix the shipped-rung posting probability only to an order of magnitude: at the A9 rate of about 5 per 1,000 the expected count is 5 and the interval spans roughly 2 to 12 per 1,000, so this campaign can say whether the merged chain posts at a few per 1,000, a few per 100 or a few per 10, and cannot separate A9's 4.19 from its 5.58. Seed blocks are contiguous from 3000 so that an extension re-runs nothing, and the shipped-rung tiers hold seeds 3200-3999 only, because a run id does not carry the tier name and the first 200 seeds at that rung already belong to the curve cells; the readout groups by platform, surveillance, release rung and epoch count, so those two tiers and their curve cells report as single 1,000-voyage cells. 4,200 distinct runs in total.",
